IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa28-part46`

-- coa28-sch1a.l4: Schedule 1A (References to people with significant control over a company), paragraphs 1 to 26,
-- lines 18665-18809 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Schedule says when an individual "X" has significant control over a company
-- "Y" (Part 1: five conditions), when a person "V" holds an interest in a company "W" (Part 2) and how shares and
-- rights are counted (Part 3). Section 790C (coa17) uses these answers; this module takes nothing from it.
--
-- HOW THE COUNTING IS REPRESENTED. A holding is a LIST OF `sch 1A block`: an amount (nominal value of shares, a
-- number of votes, or a share of capital or profits) and how it is held. Each block is treated as held by X, or
-- not, by the paragraph that governs that way of holding (11, 12, 18, 19, 20, 23). The amount counted is the sum
-- over the blocks answered JUST TRUE; the amount that might be counted adds the blocks answered NOTHING. A
-- threshold is met (JUST TRUE) if the amount counted passes it, not met (JUST FALSE) if even the amount that might
-- be counted does not, and NOTHING in between: a NOTHING block never turns into a FALSE.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (FALSE-kind comments), NOTHING
-- otherwise (NOTHING-kind comments). A route function that answers JUST FALSE says only "not by this paragraph".

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The nouns of the counting rules
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `sch 1A how a block is held` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1A para 2 held directly by X`
    `sch 1A para 11 held jointly by X and one or more others`
    `sch 1A para 12 held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with X`
    `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next`
    `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has no majority stake`
    `sch 1A para 19 held by another person as nominee for X`
    `sch 1A para 19 held by X as nominee for another person`
    `sch 1A para 20 a right held by another person but controlled by X`
    `sch 1A para 20 a right held by X but controlled by another person`
    `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by another by way of security provided by X, meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)`
    `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by X by way of security provided by another, meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)`
    `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by another by way of security provided by X, not meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)`
    `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by way of security, not meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)`
    `sch 1A another way of holding`

DECLARE `sch 1A block` HAS
    `sch 1A amount of the block` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 1A how the block is held` IS A `sch 1A how a block is held`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PART 3: SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISION (paragraphs 11 to 25), in the order of the text, then Parts 1 and 2
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---- paragraph 11: joint interests ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18710 | 11 If two or more persons each hold a share or right jointly, each of them is treated for the purposes of this Schedule as holding that share or right.
@ref sch 1A para 11 Joint interests (src:18710)
GIVEN `the share or right is held jointly by two or more persons, one of whom is the person asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 11 the person is treated as holding the share or right` MEANS
    IF `the share or right is held jointly by two or more persons, one of whom is the person asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If two or more persons each hold a share or right jointly, each of them is treated for the purposes of this Schedule as holding that share or right" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)

-- ---- paragraph 12: joint arrangements -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18712 | 12 (1) If shares or rights held by a person and shares or rights held by another person are the subject of a joint arrangement between those persons, each of them is treated for the purposes of this Schedule as holding the combined shares or rights of both of them.
@ref sch 1A para 12(1) Joint arrangements (src:18712)
GIVEN `shares or rights held by the person and shares or rights held by another person are the subject of a joint arrangement between those persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 12(1) the person is treated as holding the combined shares or rights of both` MEANS
    IF `shares or rights held by the person and shares or rights held by another person are the subject of a joint arrangement between those persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares or rights held by a person and shares or rights held by another person are the subject of a joint arrangement between those persons, each of them is treated ... as holding the combined shares or rights of both of them" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18713 | (2) A “joint arrangement” is an arrangement between the holders of shares (or rights) that they will exercise all or substantially all the rights conferred by their respective shares (or rights) jointly in a way that is pre-determined by the arrangement.
@ref sch 1A para 12(2) Joint arrangements (src:18713)
GIVEN `it is an arrangement between the holders of shares (or rights)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they will exercise all or substantially all the rights conferred by their respective shares (or rights) jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is done in a way that is pre-determined by the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 12(2) the arrangement is a joint arrangement` MEANS
    IF       `it is an arrangement between the holders of shares (or rights)`
         AND `they will exercise all or substantially all the rights conferred by their respective shares (or rights) jointly`
         AND `that is done in a way that is pre-determined by the arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “joint arrangement” is an arrangement between the holders of shares (or rights) that they will exercise all or substantially all the rights ... jointly in a way that is pre-determined by the arrangement" (a quoted-term definition read as closed: marginal reading M2)

-- ---- paragraph 21: "arrangement" (read before 12(3) and 20(2), which use it) ------------------------------------

-- src:18756 | 21 (1) “Arrangement” includes—
-- src:18757 | (a) any scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable, and
-- src:18758 | (b) any convention, custom or practice of any kind.
@ref sch 1A para 21(1) Meaning of arrangement (src:18756-18758)
GIVEN `it is a scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a convention, custom or practice of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 21(1) the thing is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF `it is a scheme, agreement or understanding, whether or not it is legally enforceable` OR `it is a convention, custom or practice of any kind`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Arrangement” includes"

-- src:18759 | (2) But something does not count as an arrangement unless there is at least some degree of stability about it (whether by its nature or terms, the time it has been in existence or otherwise).
@ref sch 1A para 21(2) Meaning of arrangement (src:18759)
GIVEN `there is at least some degree of stability about it (whether by its nature or terms, the time it has been in existence or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 21(2) the thing counts as an arrangement` MEANS
    IF `there is at least some degree of stability about it (whether by its nature or terms, the time it has been in existence or otherwise)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph says what does not count, not what does
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "something does not count as an arrangement unless there is at least some degree of stability about it"

-- Gathering (ruling E1, option B): the "unless" of 21(2) wins over the "includes" of 21(1).
GIVEN `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 21 the thing is an arrangement for this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "something does not count as an arrangement unless there is at least some degree of stability about it"
    ELSE `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)`

-- src:18714 | (3) “Arrangement” has the meaning given by paragraph 21.
@ref sch 1A para 12(3) Joint arrangements (src:18714)
GIVEN `the thing is an arrangement for this Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 12(3) the thing is an arrangement as paragraph 21 gives the meaning` MEANS `the thing is an arrangement for this Schedule`

-- ---- paragraph 13: calculating shareholdings ------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18716 | 13 (1) In relation to a legal entity that has a share capital, a reference to holding “more than 25% of the shares” in that entity is to holding shares comprised in the issued share capital of that entity of a nominal value exceeding (in aggregate) 25% of that share capital.
@ref sch 1A para 13(1) Calculating shareholdings (src:18716)
GIVEN `the aggregate nominal value of the shares comprised in the issued share capital that the person is treated as holding` IS A NUMBER
      `the further aggregate nominal value that might also be so treated` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the issued share capital` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 13(1) the person holds more than 25% of the shares in the legal entity that has a share capital` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the aggregate nominal value of the shares comprised in the issued share capital that the person is treated as holding` TIMES 4 GREATER THAN `the nominal value of the issued share capital`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the aggregate nominal value of the shares comprised in the issued share capital that the person is treated as holding` PLUS `the further aggregate nominal value that might also be so treated`) TIMES 4 GREATER THAN `the nominal value of the issued share capital`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the further blocks (answered NOTHING by the paragraph that governs how they are held) are held by the person
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to holding “more than 25% of the shares” in that entity is to holding shares comprised in the issued share capital of that entity of a nominal value exceeding (in aggregate) 25% of that share capital"

-- src:18717 | (2) In relation to a legal entity that does not have a share capital—
-- src:18718 | (a) a reference to holding shares in that entity is to holding a right to share in the capital or, as the case may be, profits of that entity;
@ref sch 1A para 13(2)(a) Calculating shareholdings (src:18717-18718)
GIVEN `the entity has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is a right to share in the capital or, as the case may be, profits of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 13(2)(a) the right is a holding of shares in the legal entity that does not have a share capital` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the entity has a share capital`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a legal entity that does not have a share capital" (a failed "where": the sub-paragraph does not apply)
        IF `the right is a right to share in the capital or, as the case may be, profits of the entity`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a reference to holding shares in that entity is to holding a right to share in the capital or, as the case may be, profits of that entity"

-- (b): amounts are fractions of the capital or, as the case may be, profits (the whole is 1).
-- src:18717 | (2) In relation to a legal entity that does not have a share capital—
-- src:18719 | (b) a reference to holding “more than 25% of the shares” in that entity is to holding a right or rights to share in more than 25% of the capital or, as the case may be, profits of that entity.
@ref sch 1A para 13(2)(b) Calculating shareholdings (src:18717 and src:18719)
GIVEN `the entity has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the capital or, as the case may be, profits that the person's rights are rights to share in` IS A NUMBER
      `the further fraction that might also be so treated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 13(2)(b) the person holds more than 25% of the shares in the legal entity that does not have a share capital` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the entity has a share capital`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a legal entity that does not have a share capital" (a failed "where": the sub-paragraph does not apply)
        IF `the fraction of the capital or, as the case may be, profits that the person's rights are rights to share in` GREATER THAN 0.25
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the fraction of the capital or, as the case may be, profits that the person's rights are rights to share in` PLUS `the further fraction that might also be so treated` GREATER THAN 0.25
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the further rights (answered NOTHING by the paragraph that governs how they are held) are held by the person
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to holding “more than 25% of the shares” in that entity is to holding a right or rights to share in more than 25% of the capital or, as the case may be, profits of that entity"

-- ---- paragraph 14: voting rights ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18721 | 14 (1) A reference to the voting rights in a legal entity is to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares (or, in the case of an entity not having a share capital, on members) to vote at general meetings of the entity on all or substantially all matters.
@ref sch 1A para 14(1) Voting rights (src:18721)
GIVEN `the right is conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares (or, in the case of an entity not having a share capital, on members) to vote at general meetings of the entity on all or substantially all matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 14(1) the right is a voting right in the legal entity` MEANS
    IF `the right is conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares (or, in the case of an entity not having a share capital, on members) to vote at general meetings of the entity on all or substantially all matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to the voting rights in a legal entity is to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares (or, in the case of an entity not having a share capital, on members) to vote at general meetings of the entity on all or substantially all matters"

-- src:18722 | (2) In relation to a legal entity that does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights—
-- src:18723 | (a) a reference to exercising voting rights in the entity is to be read as a reference to exercising rights in relation to the entity that are equivalent to those of a person entitled to exercise voting rights in a company;
@ref sch 1A para 14(2)(a) Voting rights (src:18722-18723)
GIVEN `the entity does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is equivalent to those of a person entitled to exercise voting rights in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 14(2)(a) the right is a right of exercising voting rights in the entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the entity does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a legal entity that does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights" (a failed "where")
        IF `the right is equivalent to those of a person entitled to exercise voting rights in a company`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to be read as a reference to exercising rights in relation to the entity that are equivalent to those of a person entitled to exercise voting rights in a company"

-- src:18722 | (2) In relation to a legal entity that does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights—
-- src:18724 | (b) a reference to exercising more than 25% of the voting rights in the entity is to be read as a reference to exercising the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution.
@ref sch 1A para 14(2)(b) Voting rights (src:18722 and src:18724)
GIVEN `the entity does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 14(2)(b) the person exercises more than 25% of the voting rights in the entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the entity does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a legal entity that does not have general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights" (a failed "where")
        IF `the person has the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to exercising more than 25% of the voting rights in the entity is to be read as a reference to exercising the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution"

-- ---- paragraph 15: voting rights held by the entity itself --------------------------------------------------

-- src:18725 | 15 In applying this Schedule, the voting rights in a legal entity are to be reduced by any rights held by the entity itself.
@ref sch 1A para 15 Voting rights (src:18725)
GIVEN `the voting rights in the legal entity` IS A NUMBER
      `the rights held by the entity itself` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1A para 15 the voting rights in the legal entity, reduced by the rights held by the entity itself` MEANS
    `the voting rights in the legal entity` MINUS `the rights held by the entity itself`

-- ---- paragraphs 16 and 17: the board of directors -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18728 | 17 References to a board of directors, in the case of an entity that does not have such a board, are to be read as references to the equivalent management body of that entity.
@ref sch 1A para 17 Rights to appoint or remove members of the board (src:18728)
GIVEN `the entity has a board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 17 the reference to a board of directors is read as a reference to the equivalent management body` MEANS
    IF `the entity has a board of directors`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an entity that does not have such a board" (a failed "where")
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:18727 | 16 A reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of a legal entity is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all or substantially all matters.
@ref sch 1A para 16 Rights to appoint or remove members of the board (src:18727)
GIVEN `the voting rights at meetings of the board, on all or substantially all matters, held by the directors the person has the right to appoint or remove` IS A NUMBER
      `the further such voting rights that might also be counted` IS A NUMBER
      `all the voting rights at meetings of the board on all or substantially all matters` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 16 the person has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the voting rights at meetings of the board, on all or substantially all matters, held by the directors the person has the right to appoint or remove` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `all the voting rights at meetings of the board on all or substantially all matters`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the voting rights at meetings of the board, on all or substantially all matters, held by the directors the person has the right to appoint or remove` PLUS `the further such voting rights that might also be counted`) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `all the voting rights at meetings of the board on all or substantially all matters`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the further rights are held by the person
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of a legal entity is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all or substantially all matters"

-- ---- paragraph 18: shares or rights held "indirectly" -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18740 | (3) For these purposes, A has a “majority stake” in B if—
-- src:18741 | (a) A holds a majority of the voting rights in B,
-- src:18742 | (b) A is a member of B and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of B,
-- src:18743 | (c) A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B, or
-- src:18744 | (d) A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B.
@ref sch 1A para 18(3) Shares or rights held "indirectly" (src:18740-18744)
GIVEN `A holds a majority of the voting rights in B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a member of B and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 18(3) A has a majority stake in B` MEANS
    IF       `A holds a majority of the voting rights in B`
         OR  `A is a member of B and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of B`
         OR  `A is a member of B and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in B`
         OR  `A has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A has a “majority stake” in B if" none of (a) to (d) holds (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- 18(3)(a): "a majority" is more than half.
-- src:18740 | (3) For these purposes, A has a “majority stake” in B if—
-- src:18741 | (a) A holds a majority of the voting rights in B,
@ref sch 1A para 18(3)(a) Shares or rights held "indirectly" (src:18740-18741)
GIVEN `the voting rights in B that A holds` IS A NUMBER
      `all the voting rights in B` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 18(3)(a) A holds a majority of the voting rights in B` MEANS
    `the voting rights in B that A holds` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `all the voting rights in B`

-- src:18730 | 18 (1) A person holds a share “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity—
-- src:18731 | (a) holds the share in question, or
-- src:18732 | (b) is part of a chain of legal entities—
-- src:18733 | (i) each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain, and
-- src:18734 | (ii) the last of which holds the share.
@ref sch 1A para 18(1) Shares or rights held "indirectly" (src:18730-18734)
GIVEN `the person has a majority stake in a legal entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that entity holds the share in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that entity is part of a chain of legal entities each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain and the last of which holds the share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 18(1) the person holds the share indirectly` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person has a majority stake in a legal entity`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person holds a share “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity ..." (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person has a majority stake is the answer of sub-paragraph (3), supplied by the caller
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `that entity holds the share in question` OR `that entity is part of a chain of legal entities each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain and the last of which holds the share`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person holds a share “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity— (a) holds the share in question, or (b) is part of a chain" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18735 | (2) A person holds a right “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity—
-- src:18736 | (a) holds that right, or
-- src:18737 | (b) is part of a chain of legal entities—
-- src:18738 | (i) each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain, and
-- src:18739 | (ii) the last of which holds that right.
@ref sch 1A para 18(2) Shares or rights held "indirectly" (src:18735-18739)
GIVEN `the person has a majority stake in a legal entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that entity holds the right in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that entity is part of a chain of legal entities each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain and the last of which holds that right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 18(2) the person holds the right indirectly` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person has a majority stake in a legal entity`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person holds a right “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity ..." (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person has a majority stake is the answer of sub-paragraph (3), supplied by the caller
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `that entity holds the right in question` OR `that entity is part of a chain of legal entities each of which (other than the last) has a majority stake in the entity immediately below it in the chain and the last of which holds that right`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person holds a right “indirectly” if the person has a majority stake in a legal entity and that entity— (a) holds that right, or (b) is part of a chain" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18745 | (4) In the application of this paragraph to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors, a legal entity is to be treated as having the right to appoint a director if—
-- src:18746 | (a) a person's appointment as director follows necessarily from that person's appointment as director of the legal entity, or
-- src:18747 | (b) the directorship is held by the legal entity itself.
@ref sch 1A para 18(4) Shares or rights held "indirectly" (src:18745-18747)
GIVEN `a person's appointment as director follows necessarily from that person's appointment as director of the legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directorship is held by the legal entity itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 18(4) the legal entity is treated as having the right to appoint the director` MEANS
    IF `a person's appointment as director follows necessarily from that person's appointment as director of the legal entity` OR `the directorship is held by the legal entity itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a legal entity is to be treated as having the right to appoint a director if" (a) or (b) (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- ---- paragraph 19: shares held by nominees --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18749 | 19 A share held by a person as nominee for another is to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by the other (and not by the nominee).
@ref sch 1A para 19 Shares held by nominees (src:18749)
GIVEN `the share is held by a person as nominee for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asked about is the person for whom it is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 19 the share is treated as held by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the share is held by a person as nominee for another`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A share held by a person as nominee for another"
        IF `the person asked about is the person for whom it is held`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by the other (and not by the nominee)"

-- ---- paragraph 20: rights treated as held by the person who controls their exercise --------------------------

-- src:18752 | (2) A person “controls” a right if, by virtue of any arrangement between that person and others, the right is exercisable only—
-- src:18753 | (a) by that person,
-- src:18754 | (b) in accordance with that person's directions or instructions, or
-- src:18755 | (c) with that person's consent or concurrence.
@ref sch 1A para 20(2) Rights treated as held by person who controls their exercise (src:18752-18755)
GIVEN `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only in accordance with that person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only with that person's consent or concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 20(2) the person controls the right` MEANS
    IF       `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only by that person`
         OR  `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only in accordance with that person's directions or instructions`
         OR  `by virtue of an arrangement between that person and others the right is exercisable only with that person's consent or concurrence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person “controls” a right if, by virtue of any arrangement between that person and others, the right is exercisable only— (a) by that person, (b) in accordance with that person's directions or instructions, or (c) with that person's consent or concurrence" (a quoted-term definition read as closed: marginal reading M2)

-- src:18751 | 20 (1) Where a person controls a right, the right is to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by that person (and not by the person who in fact holds the right, unless that person also controls it).
@ref sch 1A para 20(1) Rights treated as held by person who controls their exercise (src:18751)
GIVEN `the person asked about controls the right` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person asked about in fact holds the right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person controls the right` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 20(1) the right is treated as held by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person asked about controls the right` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person asked about in fact holds the right` AND `another person controls the right` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the right is to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by that person (and not by the person who in fact holds the right, unless that person also controls it)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person controls a right"

-- ---- paragraph 22: rights exercisable only in certain circumstances ---------------------------------------------

-- src:18765 | (3) “Relevant insolvency proceedings” means—
-- src:18766 | (a) administration within the meaning of the Insolvency Act 1986,
-- src:18767 | (b) administration within the meaning of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), or
-- src:18768 | (c) proceedings under the insolvency law of another country or territory during which an entity's assets and affairs are subject to the control or supervision of a third party or creditor.
@ref sch 1A para 22(3) Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances etc (src:18765-18768)
GIVEN `it is administration within the meaning of the Insolvency Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is administration within the meaning of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proceedings under the insolvency law of another country or territory during which an entity's assets and affairs are subject to the control or supervision of a third party or creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 22(3) the proceedings are relevant insolvency proceedings` MEANS
    IF       `it is administration within the meaning of the Insolvency Act 1986`
         OR  `it is administration within the meaning of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
         OR  `it is proceedings under the insolvency law of another country or territory during which an entity's assets and affairs are subject to the control or supervision of a third party or creditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant insolvency proceedings” means— (a) administration ..., (b) administration ..., or (c) proceedings under the insolvency law of another country or territory"

-- src:18761 | 22 (1) Rights that are exercisable only in certain circumstances are to be taken into account only—
-- src:18762 | (a) when the circumstances have arisen, and for so long as they continue to obtain, or
-- src:18763 | (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights.
@ref sch 1A para 22(1) Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances etc (src:18761-18763)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances have arisen and for so long as they continue to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 22(1) the rights are taken into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights that are exercisable only in certain circumstances"
        IF `the circumstances have arisen and for so long as they continue to obtain` OR `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to be taken into account only— (a) when the circumstances have arisen, and for so long as they continue to obtain, or (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights"

-- src:18764 | (2) But rights that are exercisable by an administrator or by creditors while a legal entity is in relevant insolvency proceedings are not to be taken into account even while the entity is in those proceedings.
@ref sch 1A para 22(2) Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances etc (src:18764)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable by an administrator or by creditors while a legal entity is in relevant insolvency proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 22(2) the rights are taken into account even while the entity is in those proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rights are exercisable by an administrator or by creditors while a legal entity is in relevant insolvency proceedings`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "rights that are exercisable by an administrator or by creditors while a legal entity is in relevant insolvency proceedings are not to be taken into account even while the entity is in those proceedings"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "rights that are exercisable by an administrator or by creditors"

-- src:18769 | (4) Rights that are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise are to continue to be taken into account.
@ref sch 1A para 22(4) Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances etc (src:18769)
GIVEN `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 22(4) the rights continue to be taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights that are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise"

-- ---- paragraph 23: rights attached to shares held by way of security ----------------------------------------------

-- src:18771 | 23 Rights attached to shares held by way of security provided by a person are to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by that person—
-- src:18772 | (a) where apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with that person's instructions, and
-- src:18773 | (b) where the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities and apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in that person's interests.
@ref sch 1A para 23 Rights attached to shares held by way of security (src:18771-18773)
GIVEN `the rights attached to shares are held by way of security provided by the person asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the person's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, the rights are exercisable only in the person's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 23 the rights are treated as held by the person who provided the security` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- Raised 2026-11-12 by the lead's consistency check against the "where" ruling (b) of 2026-11-05: the two arms below differ on purpose.
        -- This first arm is the paragraph's subject ("Rights attached to shares held by way of security provided by a person"), a scope limit
        -- with no "only" (ruling (c)): outside it the answer is NOTHING. The OTHERWISE arm is the "where" limbs (a) and (b) failing (ruling (b)): JUST FALSE.
        IF NOT (`the rights attached to shares are held by way of security provided by the person asked about`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights attached to shares held by way of security provided by a person"
        IF       `apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the person's instructions`
             AND `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities`
             AND `apart from the right to exercise them to preserve the value of the security or to realise it, the rights are exercisable only in the person's interests`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- limbs (a) and (b) are read together, because the text joins them with "and" (fork F5 in NOTES.md)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where apart from the right to exercise them ... the rights are exercisable only in accordance with that person's instructions, and (b) where the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans ..." (a failed "where": ruling (b); RECONCILED 2026-11-12, was NOTHING)

-- ---- the block: which way of holding counts for X -----------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN block IS A `sch 1A block`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the block is treated as held by X` MEANS
    CONSIDER block's `sch 1A how the block is held`
    WHEN `sch 1A para 2 held directly by X` THEN JUST TRUE -- the Schedule does not define "holds directly": the ordinary meaning is taken (fork F4 in NOTES.md)
    WHEN `sch 1A para 11 held jointly by X and one or more others` THEN `sch 1A para 11 the person is treated as holding the share or right` TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 12 held by another person who is party to a joint arrangement with X` THEN `sch 1A para 12(1) the person is treated as holding the combined shares or rights of both` TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has a majority stake, or by the last entity of a chain each of which has a majority stake in the next` THEN `sch 1A para 18(1) the person holds the share indirectly` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 18 held by a legal entity in which X has no majority stake` THEN `sch 1A para 18(1) the person holds the share indirectly` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 19 held by another person as nominee for X` THEN `sch 1A para 19 the share is treated as held by the person` TRUE TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 19 held by X as nominee for another person` THEN `sch 1A para 19 the share is treated as held by the person` TRUE FALSE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 20 a right held by another person but controlled by X` THEN `sch 1A para 20(1) the right is treated as held by the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 1A para 20 a right held by X but controlled by another person` THEN `sch 1A para 20(1) the right is treated as held by the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE)
    WHEN `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by another by way of security provided by X, meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)` THEN `sch 1A para 23 the rights are treated as held by the person who provided the security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by X by way of security provided by another, meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights attached to shares held by way of security provided by a person are to be treated for the purposes of this Schedule as held by that person" (so not by the holder of the security X), where (a) and (b) are met
    WHEN `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by another by way of security provided by X, not meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where ... and (b) where ..." fails for the security X provided (a failed "where": ruling (b)), so paragraph 23 does not treat the rights as held by X; the holder is not X
    WHEN `sch 1A para 23 rights attached to shares held by way of security, not meeting paragraph 23(a) and (b)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): this constructor does not say whether X provided the security or holds it; paragraph 23 answers JUST FALSE only for the provider (previous arm), and how a holder's own rights count is outside paragraph 23
    WHEN `sch 1A another way of holding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule does not say how a block held in any other way is counted

GIVEN blocks IS A LIST OF `sch 1A block`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the amount counted as held by X` MEANS
    sum (map counted blocks)
    WHERE
        counted b MEANS
            IF `sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the block is treated as held by X` b EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN b's `sch 1A amount of the block`
            ELSE 0

GIVEN blocks IS A LIST OF `sch 1A block`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the further amount that might be counted as held by X` MEANS
    sum (map uncertain blocks)
    WHERE
        uncertain b MEANS
            IF `sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the block is treated as held by X` b EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN b's `sch 1A amount of the block`
            ELSE 0

-- ---- paragraph 24: guidance on "significant influence or control" ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:18775 | 24 (1) The Secretary of State must issue guidance about the meaning of “significant influence or control” for the purposes of this Schedule.
@ref sch 1A para 24(1) Significant influence or control (src:18775)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued guidance about the meaning of significant influence or control for the purposes of this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(1) the Secretary of State has issued the guidance` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has issued guidance about the meaning of significant influence or control for the purposes of this Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must issue guidance" (a bare "must" not yet done: fork F3 in NOTES.md)

-- src:18776 | (2) Regard must be had to that guidance in interpreting references in this Schedule to “significant influence or control”.
@ref sch 1A para 24(2) Significant influence or control (src:18776)
GIVEN `the guidance has been issued under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is the interpretation of a reference in this Schedule to significant influence or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(2) regard must be had to the guidance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the question is the interpretation of a reference in this Schedule to significant influence or control`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in interpreting references in this Schedule to “significant influence or control”"
        IF `the guidance has been issued under this paragraph`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no guidance to have regard to until it is issued

-- src:18777 | (3) Before issuing guidance under this paragraph the Secretary of State must lay a draft of it before Parliament.
@ref sch 1A para 24(3) Significant influence or control (src:18777)
GIVEN `a draft of the guidance has been laid before Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(3) the Secretary of State has laid a draft of the guidance before Parliament before issuing it` MEANS
    IF `a draft of the guidance has been laid before Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before issuing guidance under this paragraph the Secretary of State must lay a draft of it before Parliament" (a bare "must" not yet done: fork F3)

-- (7): the 40-day period begins on the day the draft is laid, or if it is not laid before each House on the same
-- day, the later of the days on which it is laid. (8): the time in (a) and (b) is not counted (the intervals of s 1291(2)).
-- src:18781 | (7) In this section “the 40-day period”, in relation to draft guidance, means the period of 40 days beginning with the day on which the draft is laid before Parliament (or, if it is not laid before each House on the same day, the later of the days on which it is laid).
@ref sch 1A para 24(7) Significant influence or control (src:18781)
GIVEN `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Commons` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Lords` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1A para 24(7) the day on which the 40-day period begins` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Commons` AT LEAST `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Lords`
    THEN `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Commons`
    ELSE `the day on which the draft is laid before the House of Lords`

-- src:18782 | (8) In calculating the 40-day period, no account is to be taken of any period during which—
-- src:18783 | (a) Parliament is dissolved or prorogued, or
-- src:18784 | (b) both Houses are adjourned for more than 4 days.
@ref sch 1A para 24(8) Significant influence or control (src:18782-18784)
GIVEN `the day on which the 40-day period begins` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1A para 24(8) the last day of the 40-day period` MEANS
    `s 1291(2) the day on which the last of the days to count falls` `the day on which the 40-day period begins` 40 intervals

-- src:18778 | (4) If, within the 40-day period, either House of Parliament resolves not to approve the draft guidance, the Secretary of State must take no further steps in relation to it.
@ref sch 1A para 24(4) Significant influence or control (src:18778)
GIVEN `the day on which the 40-day period begins` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
      `the day on which either House resolved not to approve the draft` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(4) the Secretary of State must take no further steps in relation to the draft` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which either House resolved not to approve the draft`
    WHEN JUST resolved THEN
        IF resolved AT LEAST `the day on which the 40-day period begins` AND resolved AT MOST `sch 1A para 24(8) the last day of the 40-day period` `the day on which the 40-day period begins` intervals
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, within the 40-day period, either House of Parliament resolves not to approve the draft guidance" (a resolution outside the period: a failed "if": marginal reading M1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, within the 40-day period, either House of Parliament resolves not to approve the draft guidance" (no resolution: a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18779 | (5) If no such resolution is made within that period, the Secretary of State must issue and publish the guidance in the form of the draft.
@ref sch 1A para 24(5) Significant influence or control (src:18779)
GIVEN `the day on which the 40-day period begins` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
      `the day on which either House resolved not to approve the draft` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(5) the Secretary of State must issue and publish the guidance in the form of the draft` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF resolvedInPeriod
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such resolution is made within that period, the Secretary of State must issue and publish the guidance in the form of the draft" (a resolution was made: a failed "if": marginal reading M1)
        IF `the day the question is asked about` GREATER THAN lastDay
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If no such resolution is made within that period": the period has not yet ended
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS `sch 1A para 24(8) the last day of the 40-day period` `the day on which the 40-day period begins` intervals
        resolvedInPeriod MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which either House resolved not to approve the draft`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST resolved THEN resolved AT LEAST `the day on which the 40-day period begins` AND resolved AT MOST lastDay

-- src:18780 | (6) Sub-paragraph (4) does not prevent a new draft of proposed guidance from being laid before Parliament.
@ref sch 1A para 24(6) Significant influence or control (src:18780)
GIVEN `a new draft of proposed guidance is to be laid before Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(6) sub-paragraph (4) prevents a new draft of proposed guidance from being laid before Parliament` MEANS
    IF `a new draft of proposed guidance is to be laid before Parliament`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (4) does not prevent a new draft of proposed guidance from being laid before Parliament"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sub-paragraph speaks only of a new draft being laid

-- (9), second limb: "a reference in this paragraph to guidance includes a reference to revised guidance". The first limb
-- ("The Secretary of State may revise guidance issued under this paragraph") is a power: inert, reason 2.
-- src:18785 | (9) The Secretary of State may revise guidance issued under this paragraph, and a reference in this paragraph to guidance includes a reference to revised guidance.
@ref sch 1A para 24(9) Significant influence or control (src:18785)
GIVEN `the guidance is revised guidance issued under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 24(9) the reference in paragraph 24 to guidance covers the guidance` MEANS
    IF `the guidance is revised guidance issued under this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference in this paragraph to guidance includes a reference to revised guidance"

-- ---- paragraph 25: limited partnerships ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18787 | 25 (1) An individual does not meet the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to a company by virtue only of being a limited partner.
@ref sch 1A para 25(1) Limited partnerships (src:18787)
GIVEN `the individual meets the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to the company only by virtue of being a limited partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 25(1) the individual meets the specified condition by virtue only of being a limited partner` MEANS
    IF `the individual meets the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to the company only by virtue of being a limited partner`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual does not meet the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to a company by virtue only of being a limited partner"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by virtue only of being a limited partner"

-- src:18788 | (2) An individual does not meet the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to a company by virtue only of, directly or indirectly—
-- src:18789 | (a) holding shares, or
-- src:18790 | (b) holding a right,
-- src:18791 | in or in relation to a limited partner which (in its capacity as such) would meet the condition if it were an individual.
@ref sch 1A para 25(2) Limited partnerships (src:18788-18791)
GIVEN `the individual meets the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to the company only by virtue of, directly or indirectly, holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner which (in its capacity as such) would meet the condition if it were an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 25(2) the individual meets the specified condition by virtue only of holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner` MEANS
    IF `the individual meets the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to the company only by virtue of, directly or indirectly, holding shares or a right in or in relation to a limited partner which (in its capacity as such) would meet the condition if it were an individual`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual does not meet the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to a company by virtue only of, directly or indirectly— (a) holding shares, or (b) holding a right, in or in relation to a limited partner which (in its capacity as such) would meet the condition if it were an individual"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by virtue only of, directly or indirectly"

-- src:18792 | (3) Sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) do not apply for the purposes of determining whether the requirement set out in paragraph (a) of the specified condition in paragraph 6 is met.
@ref sch 1A para 25(3) Limited partnerships (src:18792)
GIVEN `the question is whether the requirement in paragraph (a) of the fifth condition in paragraph 6 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 25(3) sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) apply` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether the requirement in paragraph (a) of the fifth condition in paragraph 6 is met`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) do not apply for the purposes of determining whether the requirement set out in paragraph (a) of the specified condition in paragraph 6 is met"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph says only where (1) and (2) do not apply

DECLARE `sch 1A para 25(4) kind of partner` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1A para 25(4)(a) a limited partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 who does not take part in the management of the partnership business`
    `sch 1A para 25(4)(a) a limited partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 who takes part in the management of the partnership business`
    `sch 1A para 25(4)(b) a foreign limited partner`
    `sch 1A para 25(4) another kind of partner`

-- src:18793 | (4) In this paragraph “ limited partner ” means—
-- src:18794 | (a) a limited partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (other than one who takes part in the management of the partnership business), or
-- src:18795 | (b) a foreign limited partner.
@ref sch 1A para 25(4) Limited partnerships (src:18793-18795)
GIVEN kind IS A `sch 1A para 25(4) kind of partner`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 25(4) the individual is a limited partner for this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sch 1A para 25(4)(a) a limited partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 who does not take part in the management of the partnership business` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1A para 25(4)(b) a foreign limited partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“limited partner” means— (a) a limited partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (other than one who takes part in the management of the partnership business), or (b) a foreign limited partner"

-- src:18796 | (5) In this paragraph “ foreign limited partner ” means an individual who—
-- src:18797 | (a) participates in arrangements established under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:18798 | (b) has the characteristics prescribed by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 1A para 25(5) Limited partnerships (src:18796-18798)
GIVEN `the individual participates in arrangements established under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has the characteristics prescribed by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 25(5) the individual is a foreign limited partner` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the individual participates in arrangements established under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign limited partner” means an individual who— (a) participates in arrangements established under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the individual has the characteristics prescribed by regulations made by the Secretary of State`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign limited partner” means an individual who— ... (b) has the characteristics prescribed by regulations made by the Secretary of State"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the characteristics are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- src:18802 | (7) Regulations under this paragraph are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref sch 1A para 25(7) Limited partnerships (src:18802)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`sch 1A para 25(7) the procedure for regulations under paragraph 25` MEANS `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`

-- src:18809 | (3) Regulations under this paragraph are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref sch 1A para 26(3) Power to amend thresholds etc (src:18809)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`sch 1A para 26(3) the procedure for regulations under paragraph 26` MEANS `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`

-- Gathering (ruling E1, option B): the condition of paragraph 2, 3 or 4, after the limited-partner carve-outs of 25(1) and (2).
GIVEN `the answer for the condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (1) of paragraph 25` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (2) of paragraph 25` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A paras 2 to 4 and 25 the individual meets the specified condition` MEANS
    IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (1) of paragraph 25` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer under sub-paragraph (2) of paragraph 25` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual does not meet the specified condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4 in relation to a company by virtue only of" being, or holding in or in relation to, a limited partner
    ELSE `the answer for the condition in paragraph 2, 3 or 4`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PART 1: THE SPECIFIED CONDITIONS (paragraphs 1 to 6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each condition takes the amounts as inputs. The amounts are those that the blocks give under paragraphs 11 to 23
-- (`sch 1A paras 11 to 23 the amount counted as held by X` and `... the further amount that might be counted`).

-- src:18671 | 2 The first condition is that X holds, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the shares in company Y.
@ref sch 1A para 2 Ownership of shares (src:18671)
GIVEN `the legal entity has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount counted as held by X` IS A NUMBER
      `the further amount that might be counted as held by X` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole` IS A NUMBER -- the nominal value of the issued share capital; or, where the entity has no share capital, the total of the capital or profits in the unit the amounts use (para 13(2) takes the fraction)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 2 the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the legal entity has a share capital`
    THEN `sch 1A para 13(1) the person holds more than 25% of the shares in the legal entity that has a share capital` `the amount counted as held by X` `the further amount that might be counted as held by X` `the whole`
    ELSE `sch 1A para 13(2)(b) the person holds more than 25% of the shares in the legal entity that does not have a share capital` `the legal entity has a share capital` (`the amount counted as held by X` DIVIDED BY `the whole`) (`the further amount that might be counted as held by X` DIVIDED BY `the whole`)

-- The voting rights: the whole is the voting rights in the entity reduced under paragraph 15; an entity with no general
-- meetings is read under paragraph 14(2)(b).
-- src:18673 | 3 The second condition is that X holds, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the voting rights in company Y.
@ref sch 1A para 3 Ownership of voting rights (src:18673)
GIVEN `the entity has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount counted as held by X` IS A NUMBER
      `the further amount that might be counted as held by X` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights in the entity, reduced under paragraph 15` IS A NUMBER
      `X has the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 3 the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the entity has general meetings at which matters are decided by the exercise of voting rights`)
    THEN `sch 1A para 14(2)(b) the person exercises more than 25% of the voting rights in the entity` TRUE `X has the right under the constitution of the entity to block changes to the overall policy of the entity or to the terms of its constitution`
    ELSE BRANCH
             IF `the amount counted as held by X` TIMES 4 GREATER THAN `the voting rights in the entity, reduced under paragraph 15`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
             IF (`the amount counted as held by X` PLUS `the further amount that might be counted as held by X`) TIMES 4 GREATER THAN `the voting rights in the entity, reduced under paragraph 15`
                 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the further votes (answered NOTHING by the paragraph that governs how they are held) are held by X
             OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that X holds, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of the voting rights in company Y"

-- src:18675 | 4 The third condition is that X holds the right, directly or indirectly, to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors of company Y.
@ref sch 1A para 4 Ownership of right to appoint or remove directors (src:18675)
GIVEN `the answer under paragraph 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 4 the third condition is met` MEANS `the answer under paragraph 16`

-- src:18677 | 5 The fourth condition is that X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over company Y.
@ref sch 1A para 5 Significant influence or control (src:18677)
GIVEN `X has the right to exercise significant influence or control over company Y` IS A BOOLEAN
      `X actually exercises significant influence or control over company Y` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 5 the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF `X has the right to exercise significant influence or control over company Y` OR `X actually exercises significant influence or control over company Y`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over company Y"

-- src:18679 | 6 The fifth condition is that—
-- src:18680 | (a) the trustees of a trust or the members of a firm that, under the law by which it is governed, is not a legal person meet any of the other specified conditions (in their capacity as such) in relation to company Y, or would do so if they were individuals, and
-- src:18681 | (b) X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm.
@ref sch 1A para 6 Trusts, partnerships etc (src:18679-18681)
GIVEN `the trustees of a trust, or the members of a firm that is not a legal person, meet (or would if they were individuals meet) any of the other specified conditions in relation to company Y, in their capacity as such` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 6 the fifth condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fifth condition is that— ... (b) X has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the trustees of a trust, or the members of a firm that is not a legal person, meet (or would if they were individuals meet) any of the other specified conditions in relation to company Y, in their capacity as such`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fifth condition is that— (a) the trustees of a trust or the members of a firm ... meet any of the other specified conditions"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the trustees or firm members meet another condition is the answer of paragraphs 2 to 5, supplied by the caller

-- paragraph 1: at least one of the five conditions must be met.
-- src:18669 | 1 This Part of this Schedule specifies the conditions at least one of which must be met by an individual (“X”) in relation to a company (“company Y”) in order for the individual to be a person with “significant control” over the company.
@ref sch 1A para 1 Introduction (src:18669)
GIVEN `X is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      conditions IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 1 at least one of the specified conditions is met by X in relation to company Y` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`X is an individual`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "conditions at least one of which must be met by an individual (“X”)"
        IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST TRUE) conditions
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF all (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST FALSE) conditions
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conditions at least one of which must be met"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): at least one condition's answer is not given

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PART 2: HOLDING AN INTEREST IN A COMPANY ETC (paragraphs 8 and 9)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18694 | (2) This sub-paragraph is satisfied where—
-- src:18695 | (a) the trustees of a trust or the members of a firm that, under the law by which it is governed, is not a legal person hold an interest in company W in a way mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(a) to (d), and
-- src:18696 | (b) V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm.
@ref sch 1A para 8(2) Holding an interest (src:18694-18696)
GIVEN `the trustees of a trust or the members of a firm that is not a legal person hold an interest in company W in a way mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 8(2) this sub-paragraph is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the trustees of a trust or the members of a firm that is not a legal person hold an interest in company W in a way mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(a) to (d)` AND `V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over the activities of that trust or firm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This sub-paragraph is satisfied where— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "where")

-- src:18688 | 8 (1) V holds an interest in company W if—
-- src:18689 | (a) V holds shares in company W, directly or indirectly,
-- src:18690 | (b) V holds, directly or indirectly, voting rights in company W,
-- src:18691 | (c) V holds, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of company W,
-- src:18692 | (d) V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over company W, or
-- src:18693 | (e) sub-paragraph (2) is satisfied.
@ref sch 1A para 8(1) Holding an interest (src:18688-18693)
GIVEN `V holds shares in company W, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V holds, directly or indirectly, voting rights in company W` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V holds, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of company W` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over company W` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (2) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 8(1) V holds an interest in company W` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `V holds shares in company W, directly or indirectly`
             OR  `V holds, directly or indirectly, voting rights in company W`
             OR  `V holds, directly or indirectly, the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of company W`
             OR  `V has the right to exercise, or actually exercises, significant influence or control over company W`
             OR  `sub-paragraph (2) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sub-paragraph (2) is satisfied` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether sub-paragraph (2) is satisfied is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "V holds an interest in company W if" none of (a) to (e) holds (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18698 | 9 (1) This paragraph applies where V—
-- src:18699 | (a) holds an interest in company W by virtue of indirectly holding shares or a right, and
-- src:18700 | (b) does so by virtue of having a majority stake (see paragraph 18) in—
-- src:18701 | (i) a legal entity (“L”) which holds the shares or right directly, or
-- src:18702 | (ii) a legal entity that is part of a chain of legal entities such as is described in paragraph 18(1)(b) or (2)(b) that includes L.
@ref sch 1A para 9(1) Interests held through a legal entity (src:18698-18702)
GIVEN `V holds an interest in company W by virtue of indirectly holding shares or a right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V does so by virtue of having a majority stake (see paragraph 18) in a legal entity L which holds the shares or right directly, or in a legal entity that is part of a chain of legal entities such as is described in paragraph 18(1)(b) or (2)(b) that includes L` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 9(1) paragraph 9 applies` MEANS
    IF `V holds an interest in company W by virtue of indirectly holding shares or a right` AND `V does so by virtue of having a majority stake (see paragraph 18) in a legal entity L which holds the shares or right directly, or in a legal entity that is part of a chain of legal entities such as is described in paragraph 18(1)(b) or (2)(b) that includes L`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies where V— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "where")

DECLARE `sch 1A para 9(2) legal entity` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1A para 9(2)(a) the legal entity L which holds the shares or right directly`
    `sch 1A para 9(2)(b) each other legal entity in the chain`
    `sch 1A para 9(2) a legal entity outside the chain`

-- src:18703 | (2) Where this paragraph applies, V holds the interest in company W—
-- src:18704 | (a) through L, and
-- src:18705 | (b) through each other legal entity in the chain mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(b)(ii).
@ref sch 1A para 9(2) Interests held through a legal entity (src:18703-18705)
GIVEN `paragraph 9 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      entity IS A `sch 1A para 9(2) legal entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1A para 9(2) V holds the interest in company W through the legal entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph 9 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this paragraph applies, V holds the interest in company W— (a) through L, and (b) through each other legal entity in the chain" (a failed "where")
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 9 applies is not answered
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER entity
        WHEN `sch 1A para 9(2) a legal entity outside the chain` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "through L, and through each other legal entity in the chain mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(b)(ii)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
